memmon (2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New data sources, shown in every output mode: memory pressure (PSI),
    OOM kills plus swap-in/out and major-fault rates from /proc/vmstat,
    zram devices, zswap, the cgroup v2 memory limit that applies to
    memmon (e.g. inside a container, or any group via --cgroup), and the
    largest processes by RSS (--top, default 5).
  * Machine-readable output: --once --format json|csv, and JSON Lines or
    CSV log files via --log-format / MEMMON_LOG_FORMAT.
  * New --report DAY|FILE summarises a day's log (samples, memory used
    min/avg/max and peak time, swap, PSI, OOM kills); reads text, JSON
    and CSV logs, compressed or not, including logs from older versions.
  * Warning/critical thresholds (--warn/--crit, default 60/85) now drive
    the bar colors and, in daemon mode, alerts: level changes are logged
    to the journal and run MEMMON_ALERT_CMD, with hysteresis.
  * Previous days' logs are gzip-compressed on rollover (--no-compress
    or MEMMON_LOG_COMPRESS=no to disable); retention covers all formats.
  * memmon now reads /etc/memmon/memmon.conf and
    ~/.config/memmon/memmon.conf itself (or -c FILE), with MEMMON_*
    environment variables and command-line options taking precedence.
    MEMMON_INTERVAL and MEMMON_LOG_DIR in the environment now work too.
  * Interactive display: trend sparklines, help overlay (?), search
    (/, n, N), pause (p), unit cycling (u, also --units), mouse-wheel
    scrolling, and the alert level in the header.
  * Daemon and --plain sampling no longer drifts, and is aligned to
    wall-clock multiples of the interval by default (--no-align to
    disable). SIGHUP / `systemctl reload memmon` reloads the config.
  * All output modes are rendered from one shared report, so --once,
    --plain, the TUI and the log show the same sections; --once now
    includes the load average, and "no swap configured" is shown
    consistently.
  * Fix HugePages_* counts being shown as KiB sizes in the TUI's raw
    field dump.
  * Fix "unknown option" being reported for an option missing its value
    (e.g. `memmon -i`).
  * Fix the TUI only forcing a full repaint on its first frame; it now
    repaints fully whenever content or scroll position changes, avoiding
    garbled output on terminals with poor scroll-region support.
  * systemd service: runs as the new unprivileged "memmon" system user
    (sysusers.d) with much stricter sandboxing, gains ExecReload=, and
    reads its settings from the config file directly. Logs written by
    older root-run versions are re-owned automatically. A clear error
    now explains how to allow a custom MEMMON_LOG_DIR.
  * `make install` now points the installed unit at $(PREFIX)/bin
    (previously it always ran /usr/bin/memmon, so /usr/local installs
    failed to start); `make uninstall` stops the service and removes the
    config, sysusers entry and completions too.
  * Add bash and zsh completions, a test suite (`make check`, run during
    the package build), GitHub Actions CI for amd64 and arm64, and a
    GitHub Pages workflow that publishes a (optionally signed) apt
    repository with both architectures.
  * The flat repository now ships a Release file and can be GPG-signed
    (MEMMON_GPG_KEY) by scripts/build-deb.sh.
  * Build-Depends: libncurses-dev (replacing the transitional
    libncursesw5-dev) and zlib1g-dev.
  * License: The Unlicense (public domain), now in LICENSE.

 -- Shabbir Yusufali <shabyusufali@gmail.com>  Tue, 22 Sep 2026 19:55:35 +0000

